The experiment is set up in such a way that the control group should not be exposed to any cross-pollination comms. However, majority of the users in the control group have been exposed to cross-pollination comms, majority of which have been ad-hoc comms. Based on our current set-up, it is difficult to stop users in the control group to receive ad-hoc comms. 

Next step is to analyze the users who interacted with the tile before converting and to understanding the # of comms (both push and email) they received before interacting with the tile.

